data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":2347,"item_id":"fc_0326d6fa1befe052016adb50048a4081918e5752c158cc20c9","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"target_review\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The frozen target accurately records the approved nontrivial interpretation (locally uniform spatial constancy at q), all three hypotheses, positive n,m, interior-time scope, Hilbert–Schmidt gradient, and the required actual integrability plus differentiability/conservation—not a totalized integral. The candidate proposition P matches the stated conclusion. However closure is not established: N003 relies on unsubstantiated analysis/source applicability, so the candidate does not prove the complete target. Edge conditions include no claim at t=0 and no regularity of the scalar multiplier.\",\"locations\":[\"frozen-target.md:7-38\",\"problem.md:3\",\"source-context.md:15-27\",\"spec.json:/full_target\",\"spec.json:/hypotheses\",\"spec.json:/conclusion\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/P\"]},\"definition_reviews\":{\"D001\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Energy density is explicitly a scalar sum of squared Euclidean norms, identifies the Frobenius/Hilbert–Schmidt convention, and binds x,r with the stated domains. No theorem is built into the definition.\",\"locations\":[\"spec.json:/definitions/0\",\"frozen-target.md:18-26\"]},\"D002\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"E is declared positive-reals→R by the definition, but an unrestricted Lebesgue integral of a nonnegative measurable density need not be finite and naturally has extended-real value. The target explicitly requires proving integrability before conservation and rejects a totalized nonintegrable integral. Defining E as real-valued integral without a finiteness prerequisite/extended-real codomain is not a complete coherent definition for all allowed inputs; it cannot itself supply finiteness.\",\"locations\":[\"spec.json:/definitions/1\",\"frozen-target.md:28-31\"]},\"D003\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The Laplacian is defined as the componentwise finite sum of second spatial derivatives on the stated smooth map; it adds no PDE conclusion.\",\"locations\":[\"spec.json:/definitions/2\",\"frozen-target.md:23-24\"]},\"D004\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"The intended Euclidean/Borel/Lebesgue structure is described, but the statement identifies product one-dimensional Lebesgue volume with Lebesgue measure on R^k without a precise construction/normalization argument. This measure setup is used in source applicability and is not itself an imported theorem.\",\"locations\":[\"spec.json:/definitions/3\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/N001/statement\"]}},\"source_reviews\":{\"M001\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The supplied full telescope includes measurable/topological structures, normed additive group, measurable opens, and finite-on-compacts; the continuous and compact-support arguments are explicit. Source definition is a theorem, not a definition. Application requires the stated Euclidean volume instance.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:13-20\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/M001/source\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Function/LocallyIntegrable.lean:1-15\"]},\"M005\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full signature has two topological-space instances and compactness of both factors; the prose product statement is faithful up to product notation. No hidden assumptions beyond these.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:43-50\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/M005/source\",\"Mathlib/Topology/Compactness/Compact.lean\"]},\"M006\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Full signature/probe records required measurability, scalar and normed-space instances and all hypotheses. But the candidate's actual use must establish local a.e. strong measurability, integrability at the base time, derivative measurability, an integrable dominating function, and pointwise-in-parameter derivative on an open neighborhood. The candidate's N001/N002 formulations do not exhibit a proved integrable dominating bound from compact support and uniform-in-time support; N002's stated conclusion does not include a domination bound. The theorem therefore cannot establish the asserted derivative merely from its listed contract. Official source read confirms this is a dominated differentiation theorem, not an unconditional differentiability result.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:72-80\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/M006/source\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/N002/statement\",\"Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/ParametricIntegral.lean:13-15\"]},\"M008\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Probe gives the complete declaration including the two auto-parameterized finiteness premises; task restatement records both. Applicability is limited to finite measure and finite norm constant.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:102-110\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/M008/source\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/IntegrableOn.lean\"]},\"M009\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Complete signature and restatement include integrability on s and measurability of s; output is integrability of the indicator. This is not a general extension-by-zero theorem without those premises.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:132-140\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/M009/source\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/IntegrableOn.lean\"]},\"M011\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The complete signature requires three integrability premises, differentiability on the topological supports of the opposite factors, and a real bilinear continuous map/Haar setting. The candidate's asserted spatial integration by parts must demonstrate these premises and the precise bilinear pairing/application; the recorded source statement is not evidence that the actual compactly-supported vector fields satisfy all those obligations. No adequate completed application review is present in the material inspected. Official source is an integration-by-parts theorem, not a bare identity.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:283-290\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/N003/statement\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/N003/origin\",\"Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/LineDeriv/IntegrationByParts.lean\"]},\"M013\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"Full probe signature includes Fintype, coordinate measure spaces and sigma-finite volume. Its application and complete official declaration were not established from the available source lines; it appears unrelated to the main proof route and no inference applicability is certified here.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:223-230\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/M013/source\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Constructions/Pi.lean\"]},\"M014\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"Full probe signature states volume of a closed interval equals ENNReal.ofReal(b-a); the candidate's actual use and endpoint/order conditions were not independently established.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:253-260\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/M014/source\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Lebesgue/Basic.lean\"]},\"M015\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The complete signature is the zero integral identity with the required real normed additive group/space and measurable measure parameters.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:163-170\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/M015/source\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Bochner/Basic.lean\"]},\"M016\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Complete signature requires a pseudometric space and compact set and concludes boundedness; the restatement matches.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:193-200\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/M016/source\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/Bounded.lean\"]},\"M017\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"Probe states volume on a finite pi space is an additive Haar measure, with Fintype condition; its concrete finite-dimensional application was not established.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:313-320\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/M017/source\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Lebesgue/EqHaar.lean\"]},\"M018\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"Full signature requires a T2 space as well as compactness. The actual application and instance mapping were not sufficiently evidenced in the reviewed graph material.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:343-350\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/M018/source\",\"Mathlib/Topology/Separation/Hausdorff.lean\"]},\"M019\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"Full signature has linear order, topological/closed-Ici topology and nonempty conditions plus compactness and continuity-on-K. No actual application mapping was established.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:373-380\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/M019/source\",\"Mathlib/Topology/Order/Compact.lean\"]}},\"structure_review\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Graph includes H001-H003 and a single target P with internal producers; the AND rule means every direct input and each producer argument must succeed. The inspected closure includes N001/N002/N003, but N002's use of the dominated-derivative theorem lacks a domination bound among its stated conclusions, and N003's integration-by-parts application is not closed by the evidence reviewed. Thus reachability is not proof closure. Per-inference packet replay was not performed and is outside this requested stage.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/propositions\",\"nl0.json:/inferences\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/N002\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/N003\",\"references/audit-a.md:91-99\"]},\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/propositions/N002/statement; signature-evidence.json:72-80\",\"premises\":\"N001's continuity and common compact support on a time neighborhood, plus the M006 contract as restated\",\"conclusion\":\"E is differentiable at every time by differentiation under the integral\",\"basis\":\"M006 explicitly requires an integrable bound dominating the derivative norm for almost every spatial point and every parameter in the neighborhood. N002 does not state such a bound or an established derivation of one. Compact support alone controls support, not uniform magnitude of the time derivative on the common compact set absent a proved compactness/continuity boundedness argument.\",\"affected_closure\":[\"N002\",\"P\"],\"verdict\":\"FAIL\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/propositions/N003/statement; signature-evidence.json:283-290\",\"premises\":\"Claimed energy derivative and integration by parts via M011\",\"conclusion\":\"E'(r)=2∫ u_t·(u_tt−Δu)\",\"basis\":\"M011 requires integrability of all three bilinear terms and derivative identities on specified topological supports. The graph's provenance note is not a proof of these precise premises or application mappings. N003 is not supported by the inspected declared evidence.\",\"affected_closure\":[\"N003\",\"P\"],\"verdict\":\"FAIL\"},{\"severity\":\"definition\",\"location\":\"spec.json:/definitions/1; frozen-target.md:28-31\",\"premises\":\"E is specified as an R-valued Lebesgue integral for every admissible u\",\"conclusion\":\"E is a defined real-valued function before integrability is established\",\"basis\":\"A nonnegative Lebesgue integral can be infinite; the task explicitly requires actual integrability and rejects reliance on totalization. The definition does not encode an extended-real value or a finiteness guard.\",\"affected_closure\":[\"D002\",\"N001\",\"N002\",\"P\"],\"verdict\":\"FAIL\"}]}}"}

